course: dictionary
lesson: 5415
title: The word lack
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lack is a word that can be a verb or a noun. As a verb, to lack means not to have something, or not to have enough of it. «Vitamin C helps wounds heal, and sailors once got scurvy from lacking it.» The sailors did not have enough vitamin C, so they got ill.
explain: As a noun, a lack is not having enough of something: a lack of sleep, a lack of water. «Billions of people today still lack safe toilets.» Here lack means they do not have safe toilets. Ask yourself: is something missing? If yes, lack is probably the word.
explain: In maths, lack helps you find how many more you need. If a team needs 10 players and has 7, it lacks 3. You can work it out with goal minus have: 10 − 7 = 3.
fact: To lack means not to have something, or not to have enough of it.
fact: A lack is not having enough: a lack of sleep, a lack of water.
fact: «Plants die from a lack of light or water.» Here lack means there is not enough of it.
fact: In maths, «lacks 3» means 3 more are needed to reach the whole amount.
fact: Phrases with lack: lack of, for lack of, and lack nothing (to have everything you need).
exercise: «Vitamin C helps wounds heal, and sailors once got scurvy from lacking it.» What does lacking mean here? | *Not having enough | Eating too much | Healing quickly | Sailing far away
exercise: A team needs 10 players and has 7. In maths, how many does it lack? | 10 | *3 | 17 | 7
exercise: Plants can die from a ___ of light. Which word fits? | lend | lace | *lack | lamp
test: «People still came, because cities had what villages lacked: jobs, markets, temples and schools.» What does lacked mean here? | Brought with them | Wanted most | Built quickly | *Did not have
test: Sailors once got scurvy from a lack of vitamin C. What did the lack cause? | Happy sailors | Lemons | *Scurvy | Strong sails
exam: Tom has 12 marbles and needs 15. In maths, what does he lack? | 12 | *3 | 15 | 27
